{"availability":"available","full":"krishnakumar4a4/tail-userspace","name":"tail-userspace","description":"Lightweight userspace tailscale networking without having to install system level VPN configuration","category":"Other","language":"Swift","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-05T18:09:24Z","updated":"2026-09-26T16:07:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A lightweight, unprivileged macOS menu bar application and shell CLI for Tailscale in Userspace Networking Mode (tailscaled --tun=userspace-networking).","Designed with UX ideas inspired by Trayscale, built natively in Swift for macOS without any Linux GTK4 or Libadwaita dependencies.","Standard Tailscale on macOS requires root/admin permissions, installs a system-wide Network Extension (VPN profile), and routes all device traffic through a virtual utun adapter."],"features":["Zero Root / No Admin Rights: Runs unprivileged with isolated state in your user Library.","No System VPN Profile: Does not touch your Mac's system network settings, DNS, or VPN profiles.","Bidirectional Port Forwarding:","Coexists with Tailscale Desktop: Can run simultaneously alongside the official Tailscale Desktop app as an isolated secondary node on your tailnet.","Native & Featherweight: 398 KB bundle, <15 MB RAM, instant startup, zero Dock clutter (LSUIElement = true)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krishnakumar4a4/tail-userspace/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6e954b033b1744564c08136260cc598d6720a83146dd0e89c4e96c0b1873ab5e","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:38:43.329Z","project